>> title: Egg Drop Soup
>> category: Soups
>> tags: eggs, chicken, chinese, stovetop, quick
>> counters: Takeout Counter
>> aka: egg drop soup, egg flower soup, dan hua tang, 蛋花湯, 蛋花汤
>> pairs-with: egg-fried-rice
>> servings: 4
>> time: 15 min
>> slack: narrow — the egg goes in off the boil; a pot still at a rolling boil scrambles it into lumps instead of ribbons

>> step: simmer 5 min, fish the ginger out
Bring @chicken stock{4%cups}(950 mL), @fresh ginger{2%slices}(coin-sized), @kosher salt{1/2%tsp}, and @white pepper{1/4%tsp} to a bare ~simmer{5%min} in a #saucepan{}, then lift the ginger out.

>> step: thicken 1 min
Thicken @&(~1)stock{} with @cornstarch{2%Tbs}(slaked in 3 Tbs cold water), ~simmer{1%min}, until it just films a spoon.

>> step: ribbon the egg in off the heat
Stir @eggs{3%large}(beaten with 1 tsp water) into @&(~1)stock{} in the thinnest stream you can pour, moving the spoon in one direction, off the heat.

>> step: finish and serve
Finish @&(~1)soup{} with @toasted sesame oil{1/2%tsp}, @scallions{2}(thinly sliced), and @frozen peas{1/4%cup}(35 g; thawed).
